---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import kyoto01 from '../assets/kyoto-01.jpg';
import kyoto02 from '../assets/kyoto-02.jpg';
import kyoto03 from '../assets/kyoto-03.jpg';
import kyoto04 from '../assets/kyoto-04.jpg';
import kyoto05 from '../assets/kyoto-05.jpg';
import kyoto06 from '../assets/kyoto-06.jpg';
---

<Layout
  title="Kyoto, Japan — Your Name"
  description="Six days in Kyoto — temples, bamboo groves and back streets."
  currentPage="photos"
>
  <main>
    <div class="wrap trip-header">
      <div class="stamp">
        <span class="stamp-place">Kyoto, Japan</span>
        <span class="stamp-sep">·</span><span>35.0116&deg; N, 135.7681&deg; E</span>
        <span class="stamp-sep">·</span><span>6 days</span>
        <span class="stamp-sep">·</span><span>214 photos</span>
      </div>
      <h1>Temples, bamboo groves and back streets</h1>
      <p class="trip-dek">A slow week in the old capital, timed around the shoulder season — early mornings at the shrines before the tour buses arrive, and a lot of walking in between.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap trip-body">

      <div class="trip-block">
        <p>Kyoto rewards mornings. Most of this set was shot between 6 and 8am, when the light is low and the famous spots are still mostly empty — by 10 the same paths are shoulder to shoulder.</p>
        <p>Replace this paragraph with your own trip notes. Write however much or little you want per stop — some days might just get a photo and a caption, others a few paragraphs of context.</p>
      </div>

      <Figure
        src={kyoto01}
        alt="Torii gates at Fushimi Inari at sunrise"
        caption="Fushimi Inari-taisha, 6:40am — the gates start about ten minutes' walk from the entrance."
      />

      <div class="trip-block">
        <p>The Arashiyama bamboo grove is a five-minute walk that everyone stops in for twenty. It's smaller than it photographs, but the light coming through the stalks around mid-morning is worth the crowds.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="photo-pair">
        <Figure
          src={kyoto02}
          alt="Bamboo grove in Arashiyama"
          caption="Arashiyama bamboo grove."
          widths={900}
          sizes="(max-width: 720px) 100vw, 580px"
        />
        <Figure
          src={kyoto04}
          alt="Detail shot of temple architecture"
          caption="Roofline detail, Tenryu-ji."
          widths={900}
          sizes="(max-width: 720px) 100vw, 580px"
        />
      </div>

      <Figure
        src={kyoto03}
        alt="Quiet backstreet in Gion district"
        caption="Gion, late afternoon — the quieter lanes a couple of streets back from Hanamikoji."
      />

      <div class="trip-block">
        <p>Kinkaku-ji is the one stop that's genuinely as striking in person as in every photo of it. Worth going even knowing exactly what you're going to see.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="photo-pair">
        <Figure
          src={kyoto05}
          alt="Reflection of the golden pavilion"
          caption="Kinkaku-ji reflected in the pond."
          widths={900}
          sizes="(max-width: 720px) 100vw, 580px"
        />
        <Figure
          src={kyoto06}
          alt="View from Kiyomizu-dera at dusk"
          caption="Kiyomizu-dera, just before closing."
          widths={900}
          sizes="(max-width: 720px) 100vw, 580px"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="trip-block">
        <p>Add a closing paragraph here — how the trip ended, what you'd do differently, or what's next. This block, and the structure above it, is the template: duplicate this file for your next trip and swap in your own photos, captions and notes.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
